# No widows on mobile

When writing or editing visible UI copy (headlines, subheads, body, footers):

- Do **not** leave a single short word alone on the last line of a block on narrow viewports.
- Prefer, in order:
  1. Intentional line breaks for paired headlines (`Clear screens` / `Careful craft`)
  2. Non-breaking spaces (`\u00A0`) before short trailing words (`at home`, `& more`, `a storefront`)
  3. Tailwind `text-pretty` on paragraphs and `text-balance` on display headings
- Check the result at a phone width (~375px) before calling the edit done.
- Apply this whenever optimizing or adding copy — not only when the user mentions widows.
